# All-player owner corner markers

Replace custom-item ownership dots with coloured corner triangles shown only in the All-player Analysis view.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] A custom Analysis row has no owner marker while one player colour is selected.
- [x] All-player mode shows an owner marker for every saved production check and plan.
- [x] The marker is a triangle filled with the owning player's colour.
- [x] The triangle fills the upper-right corner of the row's fixed left-hand cell.
- [x] The marker is positioned slightly left/up relative to the former dot while remaining inside the cell bounds.
- [x] The marker does not alter row height, name/icon alignment, expansion, or fixed/value-pane synchronization.
- [x] The marker has an accessible ownership label that does not duplicate the row action.
- [x] Switching between a player and All updates markers immediately without changing stored ownership.
- [x] UI regression coverage compiles.
- [ ] Focused rendering checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Evidence

- Replaced the inline owner dot with a non-layout-affecting 13-point upper-right corner triangle overlay.
- Restricted owner markers to All-player mode while preserving the existing accessible ownership identifier and label.
- Added UI coverage that verifies the marker is absent for a single-player selection and present in All-player mode.
- Arm64 simulator-target `xcodebuild build-for-testing` succeeded.
